The {{Term/Store|Cap of the Wind||Series, BotW, TotK}} is a recurring [[Item]] in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK}}<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
{{Descriptions BotW}}
The Cap of the Wind is a piece of [[Armor]] which can be obtained using the [[Amiibo (Ability)|amiibo]] [[Rune]] while scanning the {{SSB|-}} series Toon Link amiibo or {{TLoZ|-}} 30th Anniversary series Toon Link amiibo. Each time the figure is scanned, a [[Metal Chest]] will appear that has a small chance to contain the Cap of the Wind. It can be enhanced by a [[Great Fairy]] but cannot be [[Dye]]s at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]].

The Cap of the Wind, alongside the [[Tunic of the Wind]] and [[Trousers of the Wind]], comprise the [[Hero of Winds Set]] which resembles Link's outfit from {{TWW}}. When it has been enhanced by two levels, it provides the Master Sword Beam Up [[Set Bonus]] when worn with the full set.

====Enhancing====
{{Armor Levels|BotW|Cap of the Wind}}
{{Noncanon|End}}

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Descriptions TotK}}
{{Stub|TotK}}
The Cap of the Wind can be obtained from a [[Treasure Chest]] in the southernmost cavern below the [[Tingel Island Chasm]] in the [[Akkala Highlands Depths]] or by using the [[Amiibo (Ability)|amiibo]] [[Ancient Power]].

The Cap of the Wind, alongside the [[Tunic of the Wind]] and [[Trousers of the Wind]], comprises the [[Hero of Winds Set|Of the Wind Set]] which resembles [[Link]]'s outfit from {{TWW}}.

